            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\n        \"F004\",\n        \"F006\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposed summary changes the statutory exception ('except that if the date of the treatment requires leave to begin in less than 30 days, the employee shall provide such notice as is practicable') into an unconditional requirement ('even if the date of the treatment requires leave to begin in less than 30 days'). This contradicts the source text by excluding the statutory allowance for practicable notice when treatment begins in less than 30 days.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\n        \"F004\",\n        \"F006\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposed change populates the missing action component with 'provide' and the matching quote 'provide' from F006, where the employee under F004 is required to 'provide the employer with not less than 30 days’ notice'. The proposed meaning is fully supported by the source text, adds valid structuring without altering the faithful summary, and preserves all conditions and qualifications.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0003\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\n        \"F004\",\n        \"F006\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposed edit introduces unnecessary paraphrasing into the summary by replacing the statutory modal verb 'shall' with 'must'. Because the existing baseline summary already faithfully reflects the statutory language of F004 and F006, paraphrase modifications should be rejected.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
